.TH MYATSCC 1 "2026-10-24" "ATS/Postiats 0.4.3" "ATS2 Manual"
.SH NAME
myatscc \- compile an ATS2 file with the command embedded in the file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B myatscc
.RI [ flag "]... [" file "]..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B myatscc
is a wrapper around
.BR patscc (1)
for convenience. A file can carry, in a comment, the command that compiles
it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
(*
##myatsccdef=\\
patscc \-O2 \-o hello hello.dats
*)
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B myatscc
finds that definition in the file and runs it. A file with no definition
is compiled with the default one, which runs
.B patscc
with
.B \-cleanaft \-D_GNU_SOURCE \-DATS_MEMALLOC_LIBC \-I${PATSHOME}/contrib
.B \-o
.I file_dats file.dats
.BR \-latslib .
.PP
A file can also start with the line
.B //usr/bin/env myatscc "$0"; exit
so that it can be run as a script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help message.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry ", " \-\-dryrun
Only generate and print the command; do not run it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATSHOME
The root of the ATS2 installation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
myatscc \-\-dry hello.dats   # print the command
myatscc hello.dats           # compile hello.dats
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patscc (1),
.BR patsopt (1)
